           Multi Head Attention :   A single attention head computes one type of relationship across the sequence. But language is structured along many simultaneous dimensions: syntax, semantics, coreference, local proximity, and more. A single head must represent all of these with
             one set of Q, K, V projections, which forces it to average across different types of relationships.


    What is GQA and why does every modern LLM use it?#

        Standard multi-head attention (MHA) gives every attention head its own independent
        K and V projections. During inference, to avoid recomputing K and V for every previously seen token at each generation step, these are cached: this is the KV-cache. Its memory cost scales as h × sequence_length × d_head × 2, which for a 70B model with 64 heads at 128k context often
        exceeds the model weights themselves, simultaneously limiting both batch size and context length.

Grouped Query Attention (GQA) is the practical middle ground: heads are divided into g groups,
 each sharing one K/V head, shrinking the cache by h/g. At the extremes,
  g=h is standard MHA and g=1 is MQA. GQA retains most of MHA's
   quality while cutting memory significantly — empirically,
   8 query heads per KV group matches MHA on most benchmarks —
   which is why it has become the default for every major model since 2023,
    including Llama 2 (70B only),
     Llama 3 (all sizes),
      Llama 4 Scout and Maverick, Mistral 7B, Gemma, and Falcon (40B/175B).


 Positional Encoding: Self attendtion treats the input as a set instead of sequesnce. Opration is
 a permutation equiv : shuffling the input tokens produces the same output , just in different order.
  This means “the cat chased the dog” and “the dog chased the cat” are indistinguishable to the model without explicit position information.
 It is a property of the operation itself: without positional encoding, the model has no
 mechanism to distinguish position 1 from position 10. Positional encoding fixes this
  by injecting order into the token representations before they enter the attention layers.

  Orginal transformer used sine and cosine..Added to the attention tokens,  GPT-2 and BERT replaced these with learned positional embeddings,
  a simple trainable lookup table where each position gets its own vector.

  Rotary Position Embedding (RoPE), introduced in 2021,
  is now the standard for modern LLMs.
  The key insight is to encode position by
  rotating the Q and K vectors rather than adding anything to the embeddings.
  Each position i applies a rotation matrix to Qi and Kj such that
        qi*Kj = f(i-j)








